Third-party code and models

Grounding DINO -- IDEA-Research, Apache-2.0
  https://github.com/IDEA-Research/GroundingDINO
  Required as an external checkout (UC_GDINO_REPO): the deformable-attention
  CUDA op is compiled against your torch and cannot be vendored.
  `configs/model/groundingdino_swinb_dt_forward.py` overrides that repository's
  model config and is a derivative work of it.

models/gdino/lora -- the vendored part of it, and the only vendored code here
  `layer.py` is Microsoft's LoRA reference implementation, MIT, header intact.
  `multi_head_attention.py` and the two helpers in `utils.py` are adapted from
  DitHub (Cappellino et al., "DitHub: A Modular Framework for Incremental
  Open-Vocabulary Object Detection", NeurIPS 2025, arXiv:2503.09271) by the
  authors of the Grounding DINO fork this work fine-tunes, and carry that
  attribution in their headers.
  https://github.com/chiara-cap/dithub
  Carried rather than imported because the fork never committed them: without
  them the published adapters cannot be loaded at all.

GLIP -- Microsoft, MIT (original) / mmdetection, Apache-2.0 (the port used here)
  https://github.com/microsoft/GLIP
  https://github.com/open-mmlab/mmdetection

OWLv2 -- Google Research, Apache-2.0, via HuggingFace transformers
  https://github.com/google-research/scenic/tree/main/scenic/projects/owl_vit

OmDet-Turbo -- OmAI Lab, Apache-2.0, via HuggingFace transformers
  https://github.com/om-ai-lab/OmDet

Model weights carry their own licences and are downloaded, not redistributed
here. Check each before use; a licence that permits research use does not
always permit deployment.

